# Phase 6, fleets may change the same files: two fleets' workers change one
# file while both are still at work. The orchestrator's look finds it, and
# both leaders are told at once, each of the other.
agent G1.1: listen
agent G2.1: listen
agent B1.1: edit cart.txt | commit | progress 50 "the cart is changed" | hang
agent S1.1: edit cart.txt | commit | progress 50 "the cart is changed" | hang
file brief.md: Target: the shop | Change: your part | Constraints: none | Ownership: your own files | Acceptance: the check passes
git
orch: init
human: set fleets.mode on
orch: run new "the shop, by fleets"                 -> expect r1
task G1 "Build billing" --name "billing one" --fleet billing --check "exit 0" --brief brief.md
task G2 "Build search" --name "search one" --fleet search --check "exit 0" --brief brief.md
orch: start G1                                      -> expect "(G1.1)"
orch: start G2                                      -> expect "(G2.1)"
as-worker G1.1: task add B1 "Refunds" --name "refund flow" --owns refunds.txt --check "exit 0" --brief brief.md
as-worker G2.1: task add S1 "The box" --name "search box" --owns search.txt --check "exit 0" --brief brief.md
as-worker G1.1: start B1                            -> expect "(B1.1)"
as-worker G2.1: start S1                            -> expect "(S1.1)"
await: in r2: B1.1 progress.pct 50; in r3: S1.1 progress.pct 50
clock +6m
orch: wait --timeout 10                             -> expect overlap "billing's B1 and search's S1" cart.txt
as-worker G1.1: wait --timeout 10                   -> expect overlap "your B1 and search's S1 both change cart.txt" "search's leader has been told too"
as-worker G2.1: wait --timeout 10                   -> expect overlap "your S1 and billing's B1 both change cart.txt" "billing's leader has been told too"
assert: no event lost; no event twice; in r2: no event lost; in r3: no event lost
